{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedPairingMap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedPairingMap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedStandardGeneric"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rskPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rskPair","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedPairingMap.lean#L81-L87","doc":"**The RSK pair of a permutation.**  `σ ↦ (P(wordOfPerm σ), Q̃(wordOfPerm σ))`,\na point of `Σ_λ SYT(λ)²`.  The map underlying the Robinson–Schensted\ncorrespondence `Sym n ≃ Σ_λ SYT(λ)²`; bijectivity (via the bumping-reversal\ninverse) and the resulting `Σ_{λ⊢n} (f^λ)² = n!` are the remaining bricks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.wordOfPerm_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.wordOfPerm_content","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedPairingMap.lean#L62-L79","doc":"**`wordOfPerm σ` is a permutation word.**  Its content is exactly `{1,…,n}`:\n`σ` permutes `Fin n`, so the underlying multiset of values is `range n`, and the\n`+1` shift lands it on `(range n).map (·+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.wordOfPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.wordOfPerm","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedPairingMap.lean#L57-L60","doc":"The word read off a permutation `σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin n)`: `σ(0)+1, …, σ(n-1)+1`\n(values shifted into `{1,…,n}` so the insertion tableau is standard). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rskPairWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rskPairWord","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedPairingMap.lean#L49-L55","doc":"**The RSK pair of a permutation word.**  For a word `w` with content `{1,…,n}`,\nthe insertion tableau `P(w)` and the recording tableau `Q̃(w)` — both standard,\nboth of shape `pShape w` — packaged as a point of `Σ_λ SYT(λ)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.recordingShape_eq_pShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.recordingShape_eq_pShape","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedPairingMap.lean#L39-L47","doc":"**`Q̃(w)` and `P(w)` share a Young diagram.**  The recording shape equals the\ninsertion shape: `insertWordRec_shape_eq_P` gives the row-length lists agree\n(`shiftT_shape` strips the `0→1` relabel), and `ofRowLens` of equal row-length\nlists is the same diagram (the `Sorted` proof is propositional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.pShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.pShape","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedPairingMap.lean#L34-L37","doc":"The **insertion shape** `pShape w`: the Young diagram of the insertion tableau\n`P(w)`, on its row-length shape. ","signatureChunk":0}]}